{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund a nationwide cull to reduce invasive ring-necked parakeets",
        "additional_details": "Ring-necked parakeets compete with native birds for food and nesting sites. Research shows they displace native birds from feeding sites, and Defra recognises the conservation threat.\r\n\r\nIntroduced grey squirrels and muntjac deer demonstrate how difficult invasive species can become to control once established, with serious consequences for native biodiversity.\r\n\r\nWe urge the Government to act before parakeet populations expand further and effective control becomes increasingly difficult and costly.",
        "background": "Establish and fund a coordinated, humane culling programme across England to achieve a substantial and sustained reduction in the invasive ring-necked parakeet population. Set national population reduction targets and monitor the benefits for native wildlife.",
